NOT suppress the finding (the mandatory-reason branch), alongside the well-formed-reason contrast test.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Add a narrow inline escape marker, # timing: artifact-equality — <reason>, ... A reason is mandatory.'","AC: 'contrast tests proving ... reason-required artifact-equality escapes are not flagged' — covers the reasoned form but not a reasonless marker."],"finding":"The plan makes the escape marker's reason MANDATORY ('A reason is mandatory') but no acceptance criterion proves the reason-required branch: that a marker without a reason still fires (is rejected as a valid escape). The contrast tests only cover a well-formed reason-required escape being unflagged.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f199cd52f89d753d9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Decision > 'Add a narrow inline escape marker' and Acceptance Criteria (contrast tests bullet)","norm_id":"n13b3808fe5eedf96","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance-criterion test asserting the checker still flags a comparison whose escape marker omits the `— <reason>` text, confirming the reason is genuinely required.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiab